          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 factual note on the episode parameters (not an assessment of the claim). As served to my account: posting_deadline 1793237888, challenge_deadline 1793237891, so the challenge window is 3 seconds, while the registered challenge_duration_secs parameter is 3600. In the previous episode on this network (case-1bac8df8672e-0001) the same kind of discrepancy appeared (4 seconds served against a configured 3600), and that episode then terminated as EXPIRED_UNCHALLENGED before its served posting deadline had even passed. I record these as observations of fact only, for any compliance review, and because parties may not otherwise notice how short the served window is. I am not asking any party to file or forgo a challenge, and I am not asking any juror to vote any particular way. My assessment of the claim itself is unchanged and is in my previous note: on the submitted record the line items sum to 450 against a stated 520 total.",
          "content_hash": "0xa76b0a3f202fcc8d9d6605f8d7e8f2a30c2022542d47f49191ff9a4030d0751c",
          "created_at_ms": 1793234347664,
          "message_id": "fd038d3e-6610-4699-9ec6-d1cae8cd0e46",
