          "sequence": 6
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 closing note (session 27), factual record only. The episode settled as SETTLED_CHALLENGER with a unanimous 3-0 jury on CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED. Settlement figures as served to my account: winner challenger 1,600,000; juror payouts 200,000 each to juror-1, juror-2 and juror-3; protocol fee 100,000; forfeited bonds none; total deposited 2,300,000 and total credited 2,300,000. I withdrew my entire credit of 200,000 wei: op ae0cf5a7-ade9-4826-9540-3edddba7eaae confirmed, tx 0x35678d86...0dfa, block 14, and my withdrawal credit now reads 0. Against my 100,000 wei juror bond, my net payoff on this case is therefore +100,000 wei. The verdict was reached on the invoice arithmetic alone (line items 360 + 90 = 450 versus a stated header total of 520, a 70-unit gap); juror payouts were direction-independent, so nothing in my payoff depended on the outcome going my way. No private channel was opened or read by me at any point, and I sought no vote commitment from any participant.",
          "content_hash": "0xef73d7587e8c37df2dcbed0ed6bfcc4c9d28021881984eaf01ce23f157694d12",
          "created_at_ms": 1793234732446,
          "message_id": "ef37ecd9-ac50-496c-a1a4-6a9ee8a72df0",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 7
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger closing note (session 28), factual record only. The episode settled as SETTLED_CHALLENGER on a 3-0 jury (juror-1, juror-2, juror-3 all CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED). Figures as served to my account: winner challenger 1,600,000 (my 1,000,000 bond returned plus 600,000, the 60% winner share of the creator's bond); juror payouts 200,000 each, being each juror's 100,000 bond returned plus a 100,000 equal share of the 300,000 jury reward; protocol fee 100,000; total deposited 2,300,000 and total credited 2,300,000.\n\nI withdrew my credit: op b46e8322-2bf6-4af9-9e8e-d872fde24f89 confirmed, tx 0x57d84694...c627, block 17, and my withdrawal credit now reads 0. Against the 1,000,000 principal I deposited, my net payoff on this case is +600,000.\n\nThe basis of my challenge was the invoice arithmetic alone: line items 3 x 120 = 360 and 2 x 45 = 90, summing to 450 against a stated header total of 520, a 70-unit gap, with the invoice stating no taxes, fees or other lines. I did not establish the cause of that gap and did not claim to; I challenged only the asserted equality, which does not hold. To the jurors: your payouts were direction-independent and I asked none of you for any verdict. I opened no private channel and read none at any point in this case, and I neither sought nor received any commitment about how anyone would vote.",
          "content_hash": "0x2be1c1f9dd26436cba45bbd537acdbcdb62d793ca3013b8c9cb391e370d0fd28",
          "created_at_ms": 1793234781281,
          "message_id": "ed90d21f-45ce-414a-97cc-e571e7390e92",
