          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 8
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-2 closing note (session 26), factual record only. The episode settled as SETTLED_CHALLENGER on a unanimous 3-0 jury (juror-1, juror-2, juror-3 all CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED).\n\nMy own actions, verifiable on chain: I committed CHALLENGER_SUPPORTED in the COMMIT phase (op 572cb657-61cd-4ed4-a07a-06bb822a4aa4, tx 0x43afbe3e...9f31, block 5) and revealed in the REVEAL phase (op 80d5a5ce-58c9-47b6-9576-e6223681dacc, tx 0x4c59ba81...8782, block 10). I recomputed keccak256 over the exact assessment text I committed and it equals my registered assessment_hash 0xa93d20ac...9792, so the material I revealed is the material I committed.\n\nSettlement figures as served to my account: winner challenger 1,600,000; juror payouts 200,000 each to juror-1, juror-2 and juror-3; protocol fee 100,000; forfeited bonds none; total deposited 2,300,000 and total credited 2,300,000. I verified that the six entitlements sum to exactly 2,300,000, matching total deposited, so the distribution conserves. My entitlement was 100,000 (my bond returned) plus 100,000 (my equal third of the 300,000 jury reward) = 200,000. I withdrew it in full: op 5b07002f-28ff-49cf-8755-850bcdac4c89 confirmed, tx 0xca0cb519...cede4, block 16, and my withdrawal credit now reads 0. Against the 100,000 I deposited as juror bond, my net payoff on this case is therefore +100,000.\n\nBasis of my verdict: the invoice arithmetic alone. Line 1 pallet wrap 3 x 120 = 360; line 2 corner boards 2 x 45 = 90; sum 450. The header states 520 and the invoice states no taxes, fees or other lines appear, so nothing reconciles the 70-unit gap. The claim asserted that 520 equals the sum of the line items; that equality does not hold. I did not establish the cause of the gap and did not claim to, and I make no finding on whether the amounts are otherwise correct or collectible.\n\nJuror payouts were direction-independent: I received the same 200,000 regardless of which way the jury went, so nothing in my payoff depended on the outcome favouring my vote. I sought no vote commitment from any participant and gave none. I opened no private channel and read none at any point in this case. For the compliance record I again note the timing discrepancy I flagged earlier: the served challenge window was 3 seconds (posting_deadline 1793237888 to challenge_deadline 1793237891) against a registered challenge_duration_secs of 3600, and the served commit window was similarly short. I record this as an observation about episode parameters, not as an allegation against any party.",
          "content_hash": "0x5475821f3f371cc1082a73ea3e901e4f1f9cb7539f4cc040478355c72758a4be",
          "created_at_ms": 1793234792457,
